-- Every spelling of ASSUME the checker still accepts, one per role the
-- deprecation warning can tell apart. Each ASSUME below draws the warning; the
-- section GIVEN at the end does not, although the checker meets it through the
-- very same ASSUME node (the elaboration `desugarSectionGivens` prepends).
--
-- The file type-checks: the warning is never an error, so ASSUME keeps
-- working while it is being retired (IMPLICIT-PROPS-DESIGN.md §11.1).

-- A fact left open for the boundary to supply: the warning offers a section
-- GIVEN, spelled out with the name and the type.
ASSUME age IS A NUMBER

-- A rule defined elsewhere: still a section GIVEN, of function type.
ASSUME `tax on` IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO NUMBER

-- The same job with an input written on the head: the warning spells the
-- function type out from the head's inputs.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `is large` n IS A BOOLEAN

-- A kind of thing with no stated parts: the warning offers a bodiless DECLARE.
ASSUME Person IS A TYPE

-- A name that could be of any type, so nothing can ever supply a value for
-- it: the warning offers REFUSE.
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
ASSUME gap IS AN a

DECIDE `is adult` IF age >= 18

#CHECK `is adult`
#CHECK `tax on`
#CHECK `is large`
#CHECK gap

§ `Told the new way`
    GIVEN income IS A NUMBER

DECIDE `is well off` IF income > 100000

#CHECK `is well off`
